WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.860
3.3 million veterans and counting
have served since 9/11.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.180
Around three million have decided to
pursue higher education degrees.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.600
Research from CUNY shows that
post-9/11 vets perform above

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.360
thenational average in most socio-economic categories.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.880
Between 2005 and 2015, they had
higher employment rates

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.620
with median household incomes
higher than the national average.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.240
However, over half of employers
believe that veterans don't pursue

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.080
a college or vocational degree

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.040
and that veterans don't have
successful careers after the military.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.380
The media and the public erroneously believe that

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.680
the majority of post-9/11 vets
have a mental health disorder.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.380
Unfortunately, since government-funded research prioritizes PTSD,

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.540
and since the preponderance of well-intentioned veteran legislation emphasizes mental health disorders,

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.960
the public, potential employers,
and veterans themselves

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.040
are trapped in the inaccurate and harmful broken veteran narrative.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.600
This matters. In an all-volunteer force,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.140
reputation is key to the attractiveness
of joining a profession.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.280
How we publicly portray veterans relates to

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.379
how society conceptualizes military service.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.740
Veterans are the unacknowledged permanent ambassadors of national service.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.100
Do you think our veterans are misrepresented today in media and culture?

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.640
Why or why not? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.600
Also let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.960
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

